# Date:     2026-08-25
# Result:   140 tests across 13 suites, 0 failed. 49 function rows over 5 contracts:
#           MandateManager 25, WindowHandler 9, MockUSDC 7, and 4 each for the two
#           mock registries.
# Seed:     5042002 is Arc Testnet's chain id, picked so the number is derivable
#           rather than arbitrary. The previous version of this file was unseeded.
#
# WHY THIS FILE WAS REGENERATED. The version committed in the root commit ended
# "Ran 9 test suites ... 136 tests passed". It predated ArcParity.t.sol entirely, so
# its footer contradicted the test count published in six other documents. It was
# never regenerated after that.
#
# WHAT IN HERE IS REPRODUCIBLE — measured, not assumed. Three runs were made at this
# same seed against this same bytecode. Across all three:
#
#   # Calls   reproducible in all 49 rows
#   Max       reproducible in all 49 rows
#   Min       reproducible in 48 of 49. `spendSome` alone moved: 89,794 twice,
#             87,545 once.
#   Median    moved in 2 rows — windowRemaining (21,234 / 21,277) and
#             spendAll (206,680 / 206,684)
#   Avg       moved in all 5 of the rows below, by at most 94 gas, or 0.06%
#
# The five rows that move are exactly the ones driven by the stateful invariant
# campaign: `spend` and `windowRemaining` in MandateManager, plus `idle`, `spendAll`
# and `spendSome` in WindowHandler. All 44 other rows are byte-identical across all
# three runs, including createMandate at 1,162 calls and getMandate at 15,444, so it
# is not a function of call volume. Three runs produced three distinct tables, so this
# is not a two-state flip. THE MECHANISM IS NOT KNOWN and is deliberately not guessed
# at here.
#
# So pinning the seed is worth doing and is not sufficient. What it buys is the call
# counts: `spend` ran 125,844 times in all three seeded runs, against 125,708 and
# 125,447 in the two older unseeded ones. Compare Min, Max and # Calls across runs.
# Do not compare Avg or Median across runs at all.
#
# THE DEPLOYMENT COST ROW MOVED AND THE CAUSE IS UNRESOLVED. This file used to report
# 2,557,693; every run of the current tree reports 2,557,681. Twelve gas — one
# calldata byte moving between zero (4) and non-zero (16), a signature this project
# has now seen three times. The contract is frozen and byte-identical: Deployment Size
# reads 11,964 in both, and the on-chain code length of 11,572 confirms the runtime is
# unchanged. The obvious suspect was the four ArcParity suites added since, and that
# was tested rather than assumed — `--no-match-path 'test/ArcParity.t.sol'` reproduces
# the old file's 9 suites and 136 tests exactly and still reports 2,557,681. So it is
# not ArcParity. The superseded 2,557,693 was measured on a tree that predates the
# root commit and cannot be checked out, so the 12 gas stays unattributed.
#
# 2,557,681 is now what the repo publishes. Against the live Arc receipt of 2,557,453
# the reconciliation moves from 240 gas to 228, which is 0.0089% and still rounds to
# the published 0.009%.
#
# A caveat that applies to BOTH numbers, and that matters more than the 12 gas: this
# is a MOCK deployment. Its constructor calldata is three Foundry CREATE addresses,
# while the live deploy passed Arc's real registry addresses, and 0x3600...0000 alone
# carries 19 zero bytes. The two calldatas do not have the same intrinsic cost, so
# neither figure was ever a like-for-like prediction of the live one. That they agree
# to 0.009% regardless is the finding. Twelve gas is not the axis worth chasing.
#
# Note also that a `# Calls` figure here counts calls, not transactions, and that the
# state-changing rows are transaction-equivalent while the view rows are not — see
# README.md in this folder before comparing any row against an Arc receipt.
#
